if you follow politics if you work in  politics if you report on politics you  generally understand that every American  president through foreign policy makes  decisions that lead to people dying it  could be a drone strike it could be  cutting key medical aid to another  country it could be sending people to  war so through foreign policy presidents  cause death  that's not a new thing but the Trump  administration has turned deadly in a  way that is different in a way that is  much more easily preventable  Elizabeth drew wrote a really good  article about this for Project Syndicate  and she points out that the Trump  administration has turned deadly  simply because Donald Trump ignored  readily available advice from scientists  and other knowledgeable advisors from  day one on the issue of coronavirus  Donald Trump was told about the risks of  doing nothing back in December and  January and now he says nobody knew  nobody could have imagined Trump was  given the pandemic playbook by the Obama  administration colour-coded 69 pages and  ignored it and now says nobody could  have expected this but we know  intelligence agencies were warning him  science agencies were warning him public  health agencies were telling him what  was potentially coming and he also had  been briefed his administration had been  briefed by the outgoing Obama  administration in 2017 on exactly how to  deal with a pandemic and Trump never  focused on it and he always ignored it  he dismissed the virus he said it  wouldn't be worse than the flu he said  we had 15 cases which would soon be zero  he bragged that nobody had died he said  it's under control and of course it was  all wrong and it has been deadly Trump  could have just not invoked but utilized  the defense production act a while ago  to force the production of much needed  medical supplies but he was successfully  lobbied by  the Chamber of Commerce and Industry not  to do that and so he waited and waited  and we fell further and further behind  he didn't mobilize the federal stockpile  of ventilators and other supplies later  having his son-in-law Jared Kushner  claim in dystopian fashion that the  stockpile is ours not the states in a  very sinister ominous press briefing  last Thursday and all of this led to far  more death than necessary Trump played  favorites with states regularly we get  reports that red state governors were  getting everything they asked for in  terms of supplies and equipment while  many blue state governors were not and  Trump continued and continues to blame  systems he inherited which is code for  blame Obama Trump is negotiating in some  cases against States for medical  supplies that those states need while  insisting states have to go out and get  their stuff and blaming States for  shortages that they experienced Trump is  regularly using war language to try to  weaponize the virus as a political tool  for re-election and so the decisions  that he makes have always been primarily  influenced by political calculations and  political expediency and in the  background of all of this we hear lame  economic arguments made which  essentially are arguments that say it's  okay for more people should die in  exchange for the economy the economy is  meant to be open the country is meant to  be open the Cure cannot be worse than  the disease or we can't allow it to be  worse than the disease and of course  this ignores the reality that from day  one if we had had a proper six-week  shutdown we would have prevented the  need for these overlapping partial  shutdowns  that still are going to do economic  damage but won't actually fix the  problem once and for all it's almost  impossible to do a worse job than Donald  Trump did many small business owners I  know  people who just run a restaurant would  have been able to manage this better  than Donald Trump given all of the  resources that he had at his disposal  many of which he chose to  more and if you want to play the  business game any modest humble you know  professor I had in business school would  have been able to manage this better  than Donald Trump because most of people  who actually understand business and are  good at business understand the  importance of deferring to experts which  Donald Trump seems essentially unable to  do any doctor who runs a medical  practice would have managed this better  than Donald Trump  if Trump had done nothing other than to  say I am appointing a coronavirus czar  like Ronald clean maybe Barack Obama's  Ebola czar and just let them handled it  let them handle it and stayed out of it  we would be far better off so yes  presidents lead to death through foreign  policy and through domestic policy in a  lot of different ways but the Trump  presidency has now become deadly in a  way that is very different than what we  normally say when we say presidents lead  to death through foreign policy it's  very very ugly and we don't yet know how  bad it's going to get
 

